        "id": 1330845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-13T22:47:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I do like the idea to keep it simple... what if we only have IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_x) expand to something truthy if CONFIG_x is defined?\n\nI was messing with this idea and came up with this:\n\n    #include \u003cstdio.h\u003e\n\n    #define _config_enabled(scfg, cfg) __config_enabled(scfg, #cfg)\n    #define __config_enabled(s1, s2) (s1 !\u003d s2)\n    #define IS_ENABLED(option) _config_enabled(#option, option)\n\n    #define CONFIG_ONE\n    #define CONFIG_TWO 0\n    #define CONFIG_THREE 1\n    #define CONFIG_FOUR \"CONFIG_FOUR\"\n    #define CONFIG_FIVE CONFIG_FIVE\n\n    int main(int argc, char *argv[])\n    {\n        if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ONE))\n            puts(\"CONFIG_ONE enabled!\");\n        if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_TWO))\n            puts(\"CONFIG_TWO enabled!\");\n        if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_THREE))\n            puts(\"CONFIG_THREE enabled!\");\n        if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_FOUR))\n            puts(\"CONFIG_FOUR enabled!\");\n        if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_FIVE))\n            puts(\"CONFIG_FIVE enabled!\");\n        if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SIX))\n            puts(\"CONFIG_SIX enabled!\");\n        return 0;\n    }\n\nThe main function macroexpands like this:\n\n    int main(int argc, char *argv[])\n    {\n        if ((\"CONFIG_ONE\" !\u003d \"\"))\n            puts(\"CONFIG_ONE enabled!\");\n        if ((\"CONFIG_TWO\" !\u003d \"0\"))\n            puts(\"CONFIG_TWO enabled!\");\n        if ((\"CONFIG_THREE\" !\u003d \"1\"))\n            puts(\"CONFIG_THREE enabled!\");\n        if ((\"CONFIG_FOUR\" !\u003d \"\\\"CONFIG_FOUR\\\"\"))\n            puts(\"CONFIG_FOUR enabled!\");\n        if ((\"CONFIG_FIVE\" !\u003d \"CONFIG_FIVE\"))\n            puts(\"CONFIG_FIVE enabled!\");\n        if ((\"CONFIG_SIX\" !\u003d \"CONFIG_SIX\"))\n            puts(\"CONFIG_SIX enabled!\");\n        return 0;\n    }\n\nAnd the relevant output:\n\n    CONFIG_ONE enabled!\n    CONFIG_TWO enabled!\n    CONFIG_THREE enabled!\n    CONFIG_FOUR enabled!\n\nThis banks on that the compiler will intern string literals and give equivalent literals the same address; hence, this becomes a pointer comparison between two equivalent addresses. This isn\u0027t part of any C standard to my knowledge, but any compiler that\u0027s mildly efficient should do this, including both GCC and clang. However, it\u0027s not compatible with a usage like this:\n\n    #ifdef IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_x)\n    ...\n    #endif\n\nIn this case, the programmer should just use defined instead of IS_ENABLED.\n\nAlso, does not work in the CONFIG_FIVE case above. Although, I don\u0027t expect we would see a case like this in real code anyway.\n\nThoughts?",
      "parentUuid": "a5f7a80a_64065538",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 263,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 263,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "5172d04a8d91ce7d7b56941d1ffe3dd0e7239f6d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a3232c09_077fb4ca",
        "filename": "include/common.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 263,
      "author": {
        "id": 1270601
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-13T22:56:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The compiler will issue a warning when comparing two string literals, which results in an error with -Werror. So you need to use strcmp. The compiler is smart enough to evaluate the built in and know the two strings are identical. This is essentially what this macro does.\n\nHaving #define FOO 0 and IS_ENABLED(FOO) evaluate to 0 I think is surprising.",
      "parentUuid": "0c2d71bc_5d121075",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 263,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 263,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "5172d04a8d91ce7d7b56941d1ffe3dd0e7239f6d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "919ac971_7636ce07",
        "filename": "include/common.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 263,
      "author": {
        "id": 1330845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-13T23:04:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The compiler will issue a warning when comparing two string literals, which results in an error with -Werror. So you need to use strcmp. The compiler is smart enough to evaluate the built in and know the two strings are identical. This is essentially what this macro does.\n\nA minor adjustment can get around that:\n\n    #define _config_enabled(scfg, cfg) __config_enabled(scfg, #cfg)\n    #define __config_enabled(s1, s2) (\u0026(*s1) !\u003d \u0026(*s2))\n    #define IS_ENABLED(option) _config_enabled(#option, option)\n\n\u003e Having #define FOO 0 and IS_ENABLED(FOO) evaluate to 0 I think is surprising.\n\nIS_ENABLED(FOO) will evaluate truthy, which is sane (makes IS_ENABLED act just like defined)",
      "parentUuid": "a3232c09_077fb4ca",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 263,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 263,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "5172d04a8d91ce7d7b56941d1ffe3dd0e7239f6d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "58ddf545_36517fd0",
        "filename": "include/common.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 263,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-13T23:27:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We should probably rename it to IS_DEFINED if we want to evaluate 0 as true.  That\u0027ll also nicely make \u0027#ifdef IS_DEFINED(X)\u0027 look awkward.\n\nEven though I like such a macro, the proposed implementation is fragile. When gcc/clang needs to be updated and this assumption is broken, we\u0027ll be a blocker. What is scary is tests may just pass while production code comes out unexpectedly.",
      "parentUuid": "919ac971_7636ce07",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 263,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 263,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "5172d04a8d91ce7d7b56941d1ffe3dd0e7239f6d",
